    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d340">

                <pb facs="0372" n="274" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg274"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/5398: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-10-02T21:00:00+08:00">October 2, 1930—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 4—11 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>876. Legation’s 852, September 25, 6 p.m.<anchor n="92" xml:id="d340-f1"/></p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Gauss reports that Tientsin customs will revert tomorrow to the control of
                        the regular Maritime Customs Administration, the former Deputy Commissioner
                        taking over charge.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Lenox Simpson who has acted as <hi rendition="#italic">de facto</hi>
                        Customs Commissioner for the Shansi authorities was seriously wounded
                        yesterday when attacked in his residence by two Chinese who gained entrance
                        by purporting to be member[s] of the plenary session at Peiping. Latest
                        reports indicate little chance of his recovery.<anchor n="93"
                            xml:id="d340-f2"/></item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d340-f1" n="92" xml:id="d340-f1-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg37">p. 37</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d340-f2" n="93" xml:id="d340-f2-content">
                <p>His death followed on November 11, 1930.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
